Package: keylightd
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: automatic Elgato Key Light control from camera activity
 keylightd turns an Elgato Key Light on when a V4L2 camera produces frames,
 chooses each light's brightness and colour temperature from ambient-light
 calibration or a saved preset, and restores the previous power, brightness,
 and colour temperature after capture stops.
 .
 A privileged camera monitor observes kernel V4L2 frame tracepoints and never
 reads image contents; a per-user controller owns Key Light discovery and
 control over the Elgato local HTTP API.

Package: gnome-shell-extension-keylightd
Section: gnome
Architecture: all
Depends:
 keylightd (= ${binary:Version}),
 gnome-shell (>= ${gnome:MinimumVersion}~),
 gnome-shell (<< ${gnome:MaximumVersion}~),
 ${misc:Depends},
Recommends:
 gnome-shell-extension-prefs,
Description: GNOME Shell control surface for keylightd
 A GNOME Shell extension that controls the Elgato Key Lights managed by
 keylightd from the top bar. It shows a camera-state indicator and Quick
 Settings sliders for each light's power, brightness, and colour temperature,
 plus save and apply actions for the keylightd preset.
 .
 The indicator and its Quick Settings entries appear only while the keylightd
 session service is available on the bus, and control is mediated entirely by
 the per-user controller.
